From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: fix PCS lookup (pass consumer fwnode)

fwnode_pcs_get() parses the "pcs-handle" property of the fwnode handed to
it, so airoha_pcs_get() must pass the consumer (MAC) node.  The driver
instead resolved the reference first with fwnode_find_reference() and
then passed the PCS node itself, making the framework search for
"pcs-handle" inside the PCS node, which always fails.  port->pcs ended up
NULL, phylink then ran the 2500base-x link with SPEED_UNKNOWN (-1) and the
interface reported carrier while passing no frames at all (RX/TX = 0).

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 10:49:14.418247915 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-10 10:49:14.418247915 +0800
@@ -2943,17 +2943,23 @@
  */
 static struct phylink_pcs *airoha_pcs_get(struct device_node *np)
 {
-	struct fwnode_handle *pcs_fwnode;
 	struct phylink_pcs *pcs;
 
-	pcs_fwnode = fwnode_find_reference(of_fwnode_handle(np), "pcs-handle", 0);
-	if (IS_ERR(pcs_fwnode))
+	/* fwnode_pcs_get() parses the "pcs-handle" property of the fwnode it
+	 * is given, so it must be handed the *consumer* node (the MAC node),
+	 * not the already-resolved PCS node.  Passing the resolved node makes
+	 * the framework look for "pcs-handle" inside the PCS node itself,
+	 * which fails and leaves port->pcs NULL -> phylink then runs the
+	 * 2500base-x link with speed SPEED_UNKNOWN and no frame ever moves.
+	 */
+	pcs = fwnode_pcs_get(of_fwnode_handle(np), 0);
+	if (IS_ERR(pcs)) {
+		pr_debug("[DBG14] %pOF: fwnode_pcs_get failed: %ld\n",
+			np, PTR_ERR(pcs));
 		return NULL;
+	}
 
-	pcs = fwnode_pcs_get(pcs_fwnode, 0);
-	fwnode_handle_put(pcs_fwnode);
-	if (IS_ERR(pcs))
-		return NULL;
+	pr_debug("[DBG14] %pOF: pcs resolved OK\n", np);
 
 	return pcs;
 }
